  <section id="snapshot">
    <div class="section-num">§ 01</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">The role, <em>at a glance</em></h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Before any answer is written, the role must be understood as the hiring manager understands it. This is a hybrid business-development / marketing role with a clear bias toward execution, pipeline ownership, and cross-functional negotiation.</p>

    <div class="snapshot-grid">
      <div class="snapshot-card">
        <h3>Core Mandate</h3>
        <p>Identify, negotiate, and manage strategic partnerships across banking, FMCG, technology, entertainment, and real estate that grow Talabat's brand presence and revenue in Egypt.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="snapshot-card">
        <h3>Day-to-Day Reality</h3>
        <p>Pipeline-building, lead-gen, contract negotiation, co-marketing campaign management, performance reporting, and constant cross-functional coordination with finance, legal, tech, and regional teams.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="snapshot-card">
        <h3>Hard Requirements</h3>
        <p><strong>4+ years</strong> in marketing, BD, or account management. Bachelor's degree, excellent English, strong Excel and presentation skills, sharp negotiation instincts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="snapshot-card">
        <h3>Soft Signals They Want</h3>
        <p>"Brand ambassador" mindset, comfort in ambiguity, comfort owning a number, and the maturity to manage senior external stakeholders without escalating every detail upward.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout pro">
      <div class="callout-title">Why this role exists now</div>
      <p>Talabat Egypt is defending its leadership against <strong>Rabbit, Breadfast, Carrefour Now</strong>, and the imminent entry of <strong>Keeta</strong> (Meituan) within the next ~6 months. Partnerships are one of the cheapest, fastest levers to lock in differentiation through banking promos (CIB, NBE, Vodafone Cash), FMCG bundles (P&amp;G, Unilever, Nestlé), and category exclusives. Whoever owns this role owns a real lever.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

